<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/208084575%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Late Antique domus";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/821658053%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The structure that now stands at Via in Selci no. 82 in the city of Rome rests on the structural remains of a late Roman building that likely date to the fourth or fifth century. These structural remains are likely those of the basilical hall that often was part of a Late Antique domus.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/208084575> .

