<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/218742082%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Oluz Höyük";
    rdfs:comment "Mound site in Amasya province, Turkey. First inhabited in the Early Bronze Age (ca. 4500 BCE), the site was abandoned sometime during the Hittite Period (15th-13th centuries BCE). It was briefly resettled during the Iron Age-Hellenistic period (8th-1st centuries BCE).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/218742082> .

