<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/218832894%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Osteria Cessati Spiriti";
    rdfs:comment "In the Notizie degli Scavi di Antichità for 1884, R. Lanciani reports the find of a monolithic, anepigraphic Roman sarcophagus at the Osteria Cessati Spiriti. The sarcophagus had been discovered in a pozzolana quarry and relocated to the grounds of the osteria. Brickstamps dating to 123 CE were reportedly observed at its reputed findspot.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/218832894> .

