        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/75632296%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Clivus Salutis was a street of ancient Rome located on the southwest end of the Quirinal Hill. Its name - Clivus Salutis - is attested in Symmachus and is thought to be the same as the epigraphically attested vicus Salutis or Salutaris.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/21938933> .

