    rdfs:label "Ponte del Viceré de Ribera";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/356966898%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The bridge known as the Ponte del Viceré de Ribera crosses the Fosso di Sant'Andrea on the line of the Via Appia. The viceroy of Naples, one Parefàn de Ribera, renovated the bridge in 1568. During the Second World War, the bridge was bombed and was eventually restored in 2005.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/220822469> .

