    dcterms:description "This palace of Nebuchadnezzar II is often referred to as the \"New Palace,\" principally since it was built first the first time during the Neo-Babylonian Empire. Achaemenid-period texts referred to this royal residence at Babylon as ēkallu eššu (\"new palace\").";
    dcterms:modified "2021-01-26T11:18:26-04:00";
    dcterms:subject "ANE",
