<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/227716874%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Poggio Civitella";
    rdfs:comment "The hill of Poggio Civitella near Montalcino, Italy, rises to a height of 661 meters above sea level. Beginning in 1993, excavation campaigns revealed a series of settlement horizons dating to the first millennium BCE, ranging from the archaic to the Hellenistic periods. The hilltop was fortified during this period.";
