    rdfs:label "Temple of Apollo Patroos";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/807514119%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Temple of Apollo Patroos on the west side of the Agora of Athens was built at the end of the fourth century BC. It contained a famous statue of Apollo by Euphranor. The structure wraps around the tiny fourth-century BC shrine of Zeus Phratrios and Athena Phratrios. The existence of an earlier temple, destroyed during the Persian Sack of 480 BC, is disputed.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/240065109> .

