<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/243075423%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Temple of Veiovis";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/347036492%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Temple of Veiovis, also attested as Aedes Vediovis, was a temple of ancient Rome located on the Capitoline Hill in a location known as \"inter duos lucos\", which is interpreted to mean a saddle between the two summits of the hill. The remains of a temple podium were discovered beneath the northwest corner of the Palazzo Senatore in 1938-1939.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/243075423> .

