<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/244382592%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Rock Carvings in Tanum";
    rdfs:comment "The Rock Carvings in Tanum is a collection of petroglyphs located near Tanumshede, Bohuslän, Sweden. This heritage landscape is composed of at least 600 rock-cut panels covering an area of some 51 ha (126 acres). Many of the figural motifs are maritime in nature and pertain to the European Bronze Age.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/244382592> .

