<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/245438984%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Göbekli Tepe";
    rdfs:comment "The site of Göbekli Tepe, located in the Germuş mountains of south-eastern Anatolia, was the location of a Neolithic hilltop sanctuary. This sanctuary, thought to be a series of stone enclosures with T-shaped pillars carrying carving of wild animals, was built in the Pre-Pottery Neolithic and ranges in date from 9,600 to 8,200 B.C.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/245438984> .

