<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/246262%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Buxio";
    rdfs:comment "Buxio is one of several villas mentioned in a list of \"donatio ecclesiae\" in the \"territorio Carducino\" in the Life of Saint Didier, who was bishop of Cahors in the 7th century CE. BAtlas places it with a hollow symbol and a question mark on map 25, offering \"Le Buz, Vabre?\" in the directory for modern location. Modern Vabre is a French commune in Occitania on the Gijou river. CAG reports that the remains of a villa had been reported in the 1940s in Vabre, but without further specificity.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/246262> .

