    rdfs:label "Diniktum";
    rdfs:comment "Tell Muhammad, as suggested by textual evidence in the form of diplomatic letters, may have been ancient Diniktum, a Middle Bronze Age settlement located in the Diyala region of Mesopotamia. One of its Old Babylonian kings was Sin-Gamil.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/249999668> .

