<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/25078867%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Arslantepe (Melid)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/319432673%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/629040%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Arslantepe became an important center in the Late Chalcolithic period. With the decline of the Hittite empire, the site became the center of an independent Luwian Neo-Hittite state (Kammanu). The state became a tributary of the Assyrian empire under Tiglath-Pileser I (1115-1077 BC) and it was sacked by Sargon II in 712 BC.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/25078867> .

