    rdfs:comment "Lutibu is a fortified city in Sam'alla that is mentioned in royal inscriptions of the Assyrian king Shalmaneser III (r. 858-824 BC). It is often identified with Sakçagözü (Coba Höyük), which is ca. 20 km northeast of Sam'al (Zincirli Höyük).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/258957385> .

