<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/265839%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Cantigi";
    rdfs:comment "An ancient settlement attested by an ethnic name in a single, fragmentary funerary inscription. The 19th century findspot of the inscription, presumably in the immediate vicinity of the ancient town, was at a locality called \"Plaza de Armas\" located to the northeast of (and across the Guadalquivir from) the modern Spanish town of Espelúy (Jaén, Andalucia).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/265839> .

