<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/267277%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Puente de Cañete";
    rdfs:comment "The remains of a Roman bridge known locally as Puente Viejo or Puente de Cañete lying one mile west west of Obulco on the Arroyo Salado. The bridge may have been associated with a conjectured secondary Roman road or route between Corduba and Catulo because although unmentioned in the Antonine Itinerary, the bridge's location lies between two mentioned stations: Calpurniana and Vircao.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/267277> .

