<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/267621225%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Basilica di Sant'Anastasia al Palatino";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/971691208%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Basilica of Sant'Anastasia al Palatino was founded ca. 325 CE on the slopes of the Palatine. It is now a minor basilica of the Roman Catholic church. It is the national church for the Peruvian community of Rome and the Indian community of the Syro-Malabar rite. The original basilica was adjacent to the Circus Maximus and came to be dedicated to Saint Anastasia of Sirmium (281-304 CE.), a Roman woman martyred under Diocletian. In the acts of the synod of 499, the church is listed as the titulus Anastasiae.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/267621225> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/267621225/basilica-di-santanastasia-al-palatino> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
