<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/271535243%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Norşuntepe";
    rdfs:comment "Norşuntepe is the site of a Chalcolithic and Iron Age tell located in Turkey's Elazığ Province. Excavations led by Harald Hauptmann between 1968 and 1974 identified 40-some occupational horizons stretching from the fifth millennium BCE to the Iron Age. It is now partially inundated by Lake Keban.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/271535243> .

