<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/275736%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Tingi";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/334110567%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Tingi (modern Tangier) began as a Carthaginian colony of the early fifth century BCE. A commercial center, Tingi came under the Roman sphere in the first century BCE, initially as a free city but later as the site of a colony (Colonia Julia) under Claudius and the capital of Mauritania Tingitana.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/275736> .

