    rdfs:comment "Ad Tres Silanos is a toponym associated with the ancient city of Rome but attested in a Latin inscription found at Grottaferrata. The inscription refers to a group of three fountains known by the typological name 'silanus' located in Regio VII.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/290541807> .

