    rdfs:label "Timici";
    rdfs:comment "A Roman settlement in Mauretania, mentioned in both Ptolemy and Pliny, has been associated with a site that was known as Sidi bou Chaïb in the mid-20th century. That site is now in the territory of the modern Algerian town of Taougrite (colonial Paul-Robert), Chlef province.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/295362> .

