<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/223856812%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Gleieh";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/266535322%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413309738%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/767486703%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912849%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Gleieh (also Gleiʾeh, Glaiʿā) is a small site in the middle Euphrates region and was part of the kingdom of Suhu. The city, which is probably to be identified with ancient Kār-Apladad, was situated on the south bank of the Euphrates, opposite Sur Jureh (which lies on the northern bank). Like many towns and cities of the ancient kingdom of Suhu, Gleieh/Kār-Apladad is now underwater; the area was flooded after the construction of the Haditha dam.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/223856812> .

