        <http://viaf.org/viaf/14791213>,
        <http://viaf.org/viaf/17258746>;
    dcterms:description "Buxio is one of several villas mentioned in a list of \"donatio ecclesiae\" in the \"territorio Carducino\" in the Life of Saint Didier, who was bishop of Cahors in the 7th century CE. BAtlas places it with a hollow symbol and a question mark on map 25, offering \"Le Buz, Vabre?\" in the directory for modern location. Modern Vabre is a French commune in Occitania on the Gijou river. CAG reports that the remains of a villa had been reported in the 1940s in Vabre, but without further specificity.";
