<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/256363%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Phosphoros/Lux Dubia (sanctuary)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/256038%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Strabo describes this sanctuary in his narrative of sailing up the Guadalquivir River. His text mentions a sanctuary of Phosphorus - this is likely Diana - that is known as \"Lux Dubia\" (Strabo transliterates \"Lucem dubiam\" to Greek characters, thus λοῦκεμ δουβίαν).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/256363> .

