    rdfs:label "Albarregas Roman bridge";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/256155%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A Roman bridge with origins in the first century B.C. that crosses the Albarregas River, a tributary of the Guadiana River. The bridge was been declared a Site of Cultural Interest in 1912 and named a part of the UNESCO World Heritage Site \"Mérida Archaeological Ensemble\" in 1993.";
