    dcterms:coverage "1 mile W Obulco on Arroyo Salado";
    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/61569715>;
    dcterms:description "The remains of a Roman bridge known locally as Puente Viejo or Puente de Cañete lying one mile west west of Obulco on the Arroyo Salado. The bridge may have been associated with a conjectured secondary Roman road or route between Corduba and Catulo because although unmentioned in the Antonine Itinerary, the bridge's location lies between two mentioned stations: Calpurniana and Vircao.";
