    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jnovotny>;
    dcterms:description "The Enlil Gate, which was given the Akkadian ceremonial name Enlil-mukīn-išdī-alīya (\"The God Enlil Is the One Who Establishes the Foundation of My City\"), is the third of the eight city gates of Dūr-Šarrukīn (\"Fort Sargon\") listed by Sargon II (r. 721–705 BC) in inscriptions recording the construction of his new capital. This gate is the first of the north-facing entrances to the city.";
