<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/246139%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Ad Pyrenaeum/Summus Pyrenaeus";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/246449%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/246566%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "This Roman road station \"at the Pyrenees\" or \"Top of the Pyrenees\" is attested in inscriptions, the Antonine Itinerary, and the Peutinger Map. It was located at the Coll del Pertús, a pass now on the modern French/Spanish border, and modern scholars tend to assume it was coincident with (or very near) the modern border town of Le Perthus.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/246139> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/246151%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Agiria";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/246289%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/252173%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A Roman road station in Spain mentioned only in the Antonine Itinerary, which places it between Albonica (unlocated) and Carae (unlocated) on the road between Laminium (probably Alhambra) and \"Caesarea Augusta\" (Zaragosa). No archaeological site can yet be tied conclusively to this mansio. BAtlas tentatively followed one of the potential identifications by placing the symbol at modern Calamocha, while other scholars have suggested modern Salvacañete instead.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/246151> .

