    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/61569715>;
    dcterms:description "Ancient Toletum, located on the Tagus River, was the main settlement of the Carpetani. The Romans captured the city in 193 B.C. In 507, Toletum became the capital of the Visigothic Kingdom, and in 711 it fell to Muslim invaders. Alfonso VI of León and Castile recaptured the city in 1085.";
