    rdfs:comment "The ancient city of Rusuccuru was founded as a Punic settlement on the Oued Sebaou river. In the Roman period, an inscription indicates that Rusuccuru achieved the status of municipium under Septimius Severus, yet some sources continue to refer to it as a colonia.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/295334> .

